MY3D_PROMPT_VERSION = 'balanced-figure-v10.55-compact-human-policies'
MY3D_PAIR_PROMPT_VERSION = 'balanced-figure-v10.83-compact-pose-preserving-pair'

# Shared human source interpretation only; this does not transform uploaded pixels.
# Bind original source identities before interpreting roll or planning output poses.
MATERIAL_COLOR_POLICY = 'MATERIAL COLOR — WHOLE-OUTPUT LIGHTING RESET: Relight ALL accepted people and owned materials together under neutral white studio light, with a white seamless background and neutral gray contact shadows. Discard source colored illumination and white-balance contamination, including identity-anchor casts, colored highlights/rim light and purple/pink ambient shadows. Apply to facial skin/ears/neck/hands/arms/legs, hair roots/lengths/highlights, every garment layer, shoes, accessories, objects and shaded regions. Distinguish illumination from intrinsic color using coherent same-person evidence across skin, hair and fabrics; neutral patches may support this, but skin alone or pale fabric does not prove a cast or white material. Preserve natural complexion depth/undertone, genuine dyed hair/makeup/fabric colors, prints/markings, material differences and natural tonal shading. No whitening, tanning, uniform pink/orange beauty tint, forced black hair/white clothes or blind desaturation. Uncertain intrinsic hues get conservative inference, never retained colored lighting or a claim of precise restoration. Every color lock below means supported material color under neutral light, not cast-tinted pixels. Lighting correction authorizes no identity/wardrobe/ownership/construction change, borrowed colors or detail removal. Before returning, check the entire composition for common magenta/purple/red/blue/green/yellow contamination across unrelated materials and neutralize it consistently while keeping genuine colors and tonal depth.'

SOURCE_ORIENTATION_OWNERSHIP_POLICY = 'SOURCE IDENTITY AND OWNERSHIP: Read ACTUAL Image 1 directly. Supplied face coordinates refer to ACTUAL Image 1 as transmitted; bind each accepted identity/anchor and A/B label to its corresponding face, never reorder identities by screen position. Trace each accepted face-neck-shoulders-torso and owned shoulder-elbow-wrist-hand / hip-knee-ankle-foot chain through supported local occlusion. Map garments, legwear/shoes and held items/grips to their actual body/hand. Screen proximity/vertical alignment, overlap and similar colors never transfer ownership. Apply all same-person/panel, unknown-evidence and source-fidelity rules below. Return only the requested final cartoon image.'

PAIR_POSE_PRESERVATION_POLICY = "PAIR STANDING-POSE LOCK — HIGHEST PRIORITY: Image 1 supplies each person's identity, anatomy, clothing, belongings and contact, never scenery. Convert seated/reclining/lying or cropped bodies to complete upright standing anatomy: vertical neck/torso, level shoulders/pelvis, straight neutral spine and natural legs; canvas orientation is no pose evidence. Do not invent bends or a diagonal whole-person stance. HEAD ROLL DEFAULT = EXACTLY 0 DEGREES: head centered over its own neck, crown above chin/nose, horizontal eye line, level ears; never tilt toward the partner. Preserve proven yaw/gaze independently. Anchors supply identity/hair, never head angle; when converting to standing, align the head with the reconstructed neck instead of its source-frame angle. Nonzero roll requires the same facial midline clearly angled relative to BOTH its neck and continuous upright torso after removing common photo rotation. If either axis/comparison is unclear, keep zero; frame angle, diagonal body, gaze, hair or tilted face/crop alone cannot prove local roll."

PAIR_RECONSTRUCTION_TARGET_POLICY = "PAIR RECONSTRUCTION TARGET: Rebuild exactly the two face-anchored people as complete 3D cartoon figures. Always render both upright and standing, regardless of source posture, with vertical necks and torsos, level shoulders and pelvis, straight neutral spines, heads centered above necks, and natural leg alignment. Complete unseen regions as standing anatomy. For a source-separated pair, choose contact after preserving each existing hand action; use a eligible source-unposed arm or direct body contact; keep both heads level, torsos straight and legs in a natural standing stance. Preserve clear gaze, facial direction and held objects. Head roll is exactly 0 degrees unless unmistakable same-person facial-midline evidence differs from both the neck axis and continuous torso axis after shared camera rotation is removed; if uncertain, keep 0 degrees."

PAIR_HUMAN_ONLY_POLICY = 'HUMAN-ONLY PAIR OUTPUT: Render exactly the two face-anchored people; remove animals and all other people. Render both people standing upright under PAIR STANDING-POSE LOCK. Preserve visible inanimate belongings, SAME-hand grips and all supported arm/hand poses. Preserve existing contact; connect separated people only through pose-preserving adjacent body-surface placement under CONTACT ELIGIBILITY.'

PAIR_FINAL_POSE_AUDIT = 'FINAL PAIR POSE AUDIT — APPLY LAST: If converting a reclining or diagonally framed source person to standing, discard source head-to-image roll and align the head to the reconstructed vertical neck. A tilted source face or identity crop alone is never proof of local head tilt; only distinct same-person head-versus-neck-versus-continuous-torso axes can justify nonzero roll. Remove shared camera/photo roll. Render both people standing upright, with vertical necks and torsos, level shoulders and pelvis, straight neutral spines, heads centered above their necks, crowns directly above chins, noses centered over necks, eye lines horizontal, both ears level, and natural leg alignment, regardless of source pose. Do not cock, cant, slant or tilt a head toward the other person; head yaw/gaze may turn while roll remains zero. Every final person must stand upright in a natural neutral stance, regardless of whether the source shows sitting, crouching, reclining or lying. Keep both torsos vertical and straight and both heads level; never transfer global camera roll into the body or head. Fill cropped parts consistently with standing anatomy. For a separated pair, preserve supported arm/hand poses and connect only by moving the intact figures closer for natural adjacent body-surface contact; keep torsos straight, heads level and legs in natural standing alignment. Head roll remains exactly 0 degrees unless unmistakable same-person head-versus-neck-versus-continuous-torso evidence proves local tilt; if uncertain, keep 0 degrees. Do not copy a globally rotated photo as a diagonal figure; remove camera roll and retain natural upright standing alignment.'

PAIR_FINAL_STYLE_POLICY = "FINAL PAIR STYLE CHECK: Exactly two distinct, complete, non-photorealistic sculpted cartoon figures in one continuous portrait 2:3 composition on a clean solid white seamless background. Remove all source scenery, walls, doors, signs, furniture, objects and environmental detail; retain only the two people and soft contact shadows. Show each person head-to-feet in a natural upright standing pose. Keep a straight neutral torso, level head and naturally aligned legs; do not add a fashion lean, torso bend or head tilt without clear same-person evidence. Keep proportions along each person’s body axis, use one shared support/floor plane appropriate to that posture, and add soft contact shadows without any display base. Keep identities, clothes, objects and limbs separately owned."

PAIR_HUMAN_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE_POLICY = 'FINAL PAIR OUTPUT TEMPLATE — AFTER IDENTITY ANCHORS: Return exactly two complete distinct cartoon figures standing on a clean solid white seamless background, no scenery or display base. Apply PAIR STANDING-POSE LOCK and OUTPUT HEAD SCALE: default zero head roll under the original three-axis exception; H/F 24–26% per person. Anchors supply identity, never pose or scale. Verify the one planned source-preserving connection under CONTACT ELIGIBILITY and the four-arm audit below. Return one image.'

NO_ADDED_DISPLAY_BASE_RULE = 'NO ADDED DISPLAY BASE — ABSOLUTE: Render the complete subject(s) directly on the continuous white seamless studio floor, with only a soft contact/floor shadow. Weight-bearing shoe soles, feet or paws contact that floor directly; a source-supported sitting or lying pet rests naturally on the same floor. Never add any separate display base, round disk, circular slab, stand, plinth, pedestal, podium, raised presentation platform, mounting plate or support post, whether black, white, transparent or any other colour. The white studio floor has no separate hard-edged disk or slab underneath the subject(s). This prohibition concerns presentation supports only: preserve genuine source-owned footwear, including thick platform shoes, sole thickness, tread, shape and colour; never flatten, remove or recolour a shoe or its sole to obey this rule. Keep all existing source clothing, accessories, held items, markings and pose requirements. All existing rules for rich, varied and harmonious completion of genuinely unseen clothing remain in force.'

